Read it through the command line rather than by hand: `skraft status`, `skraft report`. A
journal started on another machine is adopted with `skraft journal adopt`. Every file, event and
refusal code: [Tracking and journal](https://sebastiendegodez.github.io/skraft-plugin/reference/run-journal).

## Models

Each agent runs on a model **family**: a tier (`economy`, `standard`, `frontier`) or a role
(`reviewer`, `researcher`, `implementer`, `planner`). `assign` in `skraft-config.json` (or in
`~/.skraft/config.json`, or an uncommitted `skraft-config.local.json`) picks each agent's family;
`models` says what a family runs on per host, with an effort. `skraft doctor` shows the
resolved assignment. How-to: [Choose the agents' models](https://sebastiendegodez.github.io/skraft-plugin/how-to/choose-models).

## Supported stacks

| Stack | Clean Architecture | Quality gates | Mocking and contract tests |
|---|---|---|---|
| .NET | `clean-architecture-dotnet` | `quality-gates-dotnet` | Microcks (default) or in-process doubles; `WebApplicationFactory` |
| Python | `clean-architecture-python` | `quality-gates-python` | Microcks (default) or respx; FastAPI `TestClient` |
| Java (Maven, Spring Boot or Quarkus) | `clean-architecture-java` | not yet | not yet |
| TypeScript back end (Node, Vitest) | `clean-architecture-typescript` | `quality-gates-typescript` (Vitest) | MSW (default) or Microcks |
| React / TypeScript (Vitest) | `clean-architecture-react` | `quality-gates-typescript` (Vitest) | MSW (default) or Microcks; no contract test, a front end exposes no API |
| Node JavaScript | — | `quality-gates-javascript` (`node --test`) | MSW (default) or Microcks |

Contract testing is off by default; a component turns it on with `"contractTesting": true`. In
DELIVER, the engineer runs the gates of each component through `skraft_repl`; a gate the
project names no command for is declared absent: SKRAFT never guesses a command.
Helpers the agents reuse in every cell live in your repository under `.repl/lib/`, their packages
in `.repl/package.json`; agents never write them during an attempt, and each cell's code is kept
beside the trace as `cell-<n>.mjs`, ready to copy into the library
([Keep your REPL scripts in `.repl`](https://sebastiendegodez.github.io/skraft-plugin/how-to/keep-repl-scripts)).

